WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.920
("Ukraine has surprised the world.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.780
Ukraine has inspired the world.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.019
Ukraine has united the world.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:22.710
There are thousands of words to prove it,
but a few will suffice.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:27.540
HIMARS, Patriot, Abrams, IRIS-T, Challenger,
NASAMS, Leopard")

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.699
Vladimir Putin thought it would be a matter
of a few hours.

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:34.090
That in just a few days Ukraine would be fully
under his control.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.930
According to his plans, the Russian army would
advance at full speed and would occupy Kyiv

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.450
within a few days.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:43.200
Zelenskiy and his government would abandon
the capital, the Ukrainian army would surrender

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.700
and everything would be ready for the victory
parade.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:50.230
Putin would have his great military feat and
Ukraine would be back under the thumb of the

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.230
Russian Motherland.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.840
("We also found some parade uniforms there,
so they expected to get Kyiv in two days and

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.840
then have a parade here.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.719
So we can say now that we have completely
destroyed their plans."

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:04.439
Oleksandr Hruzevych, the Deputy Chief of Staff
of the Command of the Ground Forces of Ukraine)

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:08.080
However, the course of events could not have
been more different: The Ukrainians held out

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.681
against all odds, international aid arrived
on an unimaginable scale, and the Russian

00:01:12.681 --> 00:01:15.720
army turned out to have more holes than a
Swiss cheese.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.720
The result?

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.990
Not only was there no victory parade, but
one year later the war rages on and Russia

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:24.520
has suffered an enormous number of casualties,
both in terms of equipment...

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.330
As well as men.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:35.409
According to existing estimates, more than
180,000 Russian soldiers were killed or wounded

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:37.450
during the first year of the invasion alone.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.939
We are talking about an average of almost
500 casualties every day.

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:45.460
What’s more, in just 12 months of war, the
Russian army has lost more generals and high-ranking

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.780
officers than in seven years in Syria or than
the Soviets did during their 10-year war in

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.780
Afghanistan.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.579
And to make matters worse, the casualties
have hit many of Russia's best-trained units,

00:01:55.579 --> 00:01:57.950
such as the airborne troops and naval infantry.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.600
But that's not even the end of it.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.250
Check out this news item:

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.840
(Russia Likely Lost More Than Half of Its
Tanks in Ukraine, Estimates Show.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.840
– WSJ)

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.719
We are talking about more than 2,300 tanks.

00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:11.470
In total, according to the count carried out
by British intelligence, Russia could also

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:17.670
have lost more than 4,500 armored vehicles
of all types, 63 aircraft, 70 helicopters,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.750
12 naval vessels and hundreds of artillery
systems.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.430
And this is only taking into account the losses
that are relatively well documented.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.030
In other words, a real disaster.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:35.530
To give you an idea, despite all its attempts
and to the astonishment of all NATO armies,

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:41.030
Russia was not even able to take Kharkiv,
a city located only 50km, that’s around

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.060
30 miles from its border and one of its main
targets during the invasion.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.010
Yes, so let's make no mistake.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:51.990
It is true that with his missiles and artillery,
Putin is destroying Ukraine – cities like

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:56.220
Mariupol, Severodonetsk, Irpin, Popasna or
Bakhmut prove it.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.260
But do you know what?

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.720
Despite all the losses suffered by the Russian
army, Putin has not achieved a single one

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.490
of his main objectives:

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:07.320
Zelenskiy's government seems stronger than
ever, the supposed unification of the Slavic

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.940
nation has been a resounding failure, Ukraine
has not fallen and to top it off, its ties

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.290
with the West are much stronger and its army
is much better armed.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.010
(Our faith has grown stronger.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.730
Our morale has been reinforced.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.960
We endured the first day of a full-scale war.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:28.870
We didn't know what would happen tomorrow,
but we realized for sure: every tomorrow is

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.250
worth fighting for!

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.630
And we fought)

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:36.940
Now, does all this mean that Russian dictator
Vladimir Putin might be willing to give in?

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:37.940
Well...

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.629
It certainly doesn't look like it.

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:46.680
One year after the invasion, according to
British Defense Secretary Ben Wallace, Russia

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.220
currently has 97% of its combat forces deployed
in the Ukrainian war.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.740
Despite this, neither side seems to have victory
in its grasp.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.090
Neither the Russians nor the Ukrainians.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.760
So the question is, how on earth is this hell
going to end?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.459
How can the war in Ukraine be brought to a
close?

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:05.980
What scenarios are on the table for the major
international organizations?

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:11.310
Well..., let's take a look.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:18.699
(LOOKING FOR THE EXIT DOOR)

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:23.400
In early October 2021, a very important meeting
was held in the most important office on the

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.160
planet: the Oval Office.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.590
Among others, the meeting was attended by
US President Joe Biden, CIA Director William

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:34.130
Burns, White House National Security Advisor,
Jake Sullivan and the Chairman of the Joint

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.280
Chiefs of Staff of the Armed Forces, General
Mark Milley.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.680
What was the reason for the meeting?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.680
Well...

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.350
Basically to analyze the latest intelligence
information indicating that Vladimir Putin

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.010
might be about to invade Ukraine.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.720
We are not talking about conjecture but about
information.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.440
The risk was absolutely real.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.540
We are talking about the beginning of October
2021, almost five months before the Kremlin's

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:56.440
troops finally launched themselves on Ukraine.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:01.620
At that meeting, as confirmed by Milley himself,
four lines of action were agreed upon:

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:09.580
First, an armed conflict between Russia and
NATO had to be avoided at all costs.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:14.060
Second, in the event of war, everything possible
should be done to contain it within the geographical

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.669
boundaries of Ukraine.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:18.940
Third, the strengthening and cohesion of NATO
was key.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.340
The phone had to be picked up as soon as possible.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.250
And fourth, and possibly the key point, not
only of the meeting, but of everything we

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:31.830
have experienced since: Ukraine had to be
empowered and given the means to fight.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:36.180
Yes, VisualPolitik community, that was none
other than the meeting in which the United

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.610
States decided that this time it would not
stand in the shadows.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.930
If Russia infringed on Ukraine's sovereignty
and freedom, Ukrainians would not be left

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:44.930
to their own devices.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.010
That was the meeting at which the strategy
was set, which then gradually evolved and

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:54.039
which, along with the solidarity of many European
allies, and above all, the tenacity, endurance

00:05:54.039 --> 00:05:59.100
and courage of the Ukrainians have caused
Vladimir Putin to run into a huge wall.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.450
("One year ago, the world was bracing for
the fall of Kyiv.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:14.419
Well, I have just come from a visit to Kyiv,
and I can report: Kyiv stands strong!

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:16.759
Kyiv stands proud.

00:06:16.759 --> 00:06:19.090
It stands tall.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:23.770
And most important, it stands free").

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:28.370
Kyiv remains free, international allies have
supported Ukraine, in total they have committed

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:33.280
more than $160 billion dollars in military,
humanitarian and financial aid.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.240
A huge amount of resources that has to be
able to cover the needs of this country until

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.870
at least the end of 2023.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.280
("Nobody thought the Russians would start
a medieval war in the 21st century.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.750
This conflict is going to change the face
of Europe as much as World War II did."

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.870
James Risch, Republican Senator from Idaho
and member of the Senate Foreign Relations

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.870
Committee)

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.940
But obviously, while the fact that Kyiv is
still free is great news, the war, destruction

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:59.210
and annihilation of lives is still a terrible
scenario.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:02.060
So the question is, what are the ways out
of the war?

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.000
Well, here are four ways the war could be
brought to an end.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.780
Of course, not all of them are equally desirable.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.340
Any one of them, starting with the first one,
would be terrible for everyone.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.600
Listen up.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.669
(1.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:20.630
LET UKRAINE GO)

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:25.270
Putin was counting on the rest of the world
to do absolutely nothing.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:29.440
That the rest of the countries would stand
idly by and watch him impose his will on a

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.370
country that he himself does not consider
as an independent nation.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.370
And do you know what?

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.129
In a way, this could still happen.

00:07:36.129 --> 00:07:40.060
Take, for example, the cases of Trump and
his entourage in the United States or Le Pen

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.190
in France, who openly speak out against helping
Ukraine.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:47.819
Of course, let's not fool ourselves, if Ukraine's
supply were to be cut off, sooner or later

00:07:47.819 --> 00:07:50.160
Ukraine would most likely end up falling.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.620
Or at best, negotiating a ceasefire, which
would be a victory for Putin and a disaster

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.620
for Ukraine.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:00.020
In fact, Western weariness remains one of
Vladimir Putin's greatest assets and explains

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.639
in large part why he is still sticking to
his plan.

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:06.629
And that is precisely why Biden's trip to
Kyiv as a clear manifestation of commitment

00:08:06.629 --> 00:08:08.040
was so important.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:11.530
Abandoning Ukraine would mean leaving Ukrainians
under the yoke of Moscow.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:15.900
Or in other words, facing a lot of repression
and purges of all kinds.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.590
The hundreds of bodies that were, in many
cases, tortured from Bucha and Izyum are a

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:21.590
good example.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.590
But not only that.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:28.759
It would also be catastrophic for the rest
of the world.

00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:32.519
Think about it, we would be telling all the
tyrants on the planet that not only do they

00:08:32.519 --> 00:08:36.450
have a free pass to do as they please when
they please, but also that [FATE ACOMPLEE]

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.770
fait accompli and the politics of force are
the best guarantee of success.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.920
Now apply that thinking to places like Taiwan,
Korea and Moldova and you have a winning formula

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.580
for the worst of all worlds.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:53.920
("If Putin wins in Ukraine, the message to
him and other authoritarian leaders will be

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.140
that they can use force to get what they want.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.600
This will make the world more dangerous and
make us more vulnerable".

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.600
Jens Stoltenberg, NATO Secretary General)

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.000
This is precisely why this option is completely
ruled out.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.040
("President Putin is confronted with something
today that he didn't think was possible a

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.620
year ago.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:17.110
The democracies of the world have grown stronger,
not weaker.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:20.430
But the autocrats of the world have grown
weaker, not stronger)

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:25.339
This brings us directly to the second possible
outcome.

00:09:25.339 --> 00:09:28.279
(2.

00:09:28.279 --> 00:09:33.470
FREEZE THE WAR)

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:37.990
First the Russian offensive and then the Ukrainian
counter-offensives, on the first anniversary

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:41.230
of the invasion, the war was already in a
kind of lethargy...

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.170
At least from a territorial point of view.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:46.560
The major clashes were limited to very specific
points such as Bahkmut.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:51.160
The Russians have sent many thousands of men
to reinforce their defenses, entrench themselves

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.250
and thus try to defend the conquered territory.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.900
It is evident that the casualties suffered
by Russia have been enormous.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.110
But Ukraine has also suffered a huge number
of casualties, both military and civilian,

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.100
and although it has received a lot of military
hardware it still does not seem enough to

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.360
clearly win the war.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.630
If the allies maintain their support but reduce
deliveries, the conflict could drag on for

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.839
years and even freeze completely.

00:10:12.839 --> 00:10:16.490
What’s more, the passage of time itself
could favor such an exit.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:21.630
Exhaustion, fatigue, loss of social and media
attention or the fear of another energy crisis

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:25.779
could lead many countries to end up looking
for a convenient way out, that is, to try

00:10:25.779 --> 00:10:33.209
to freeze the conflict and, in a sense, get
back to normality.

00:10:33.209 --> 00:10:37.170
Even if Russia ends up launching an offensive,
gains new territories and then asks to reach

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:41.339
a peace agreement, it is possible that many
countries will put pressure on Kyiv to comply.

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:42.339
And do you know what?

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:46.240
Ukraine itself may have no choice but to accept
Russia's presence within its territory and

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.070
the permanent sense of fear and frustration
that goes with it.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:52.180
("We keep repeating that Russia mustn't win,
but what does that mean?

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:56.200
If the war goes on for long enough with this
intensity, Ukraine's losses will become unbearable.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.779
A senior French official told the Wall Street
Journal)

00:10:58.779 --> 00:11:03.100
In addition, this would obviously mean much
more pain and much more waiting for Ukrainians,

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.010
and it is certainly not clear what future
this country would have.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:10.360
Could Ukraine really be rebuilt and attract
foreign capital and business if the country

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:14.520
technically remains at war, has part of its
territory overrun and the threat from Russia

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:15.520
remains?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.520
It seems hard to imagine.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.209
And, of course, we cannot overlook the fact
that the Ukrainian economy is in tatters and

00:11:20.209 --> 00:11:22.240
its infrastructure is badly damaged.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.730
In other words, that could spell doom in the
medium term.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.410
The inability for the country to ever be viable.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:31.410
Besides, couldn't Russia resume its offensive
in a few years when Ukraine is weaker and

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:35.800
they have managed to reestablish part of their
military force, even if it is just by training

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.800
recruits?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:42.560
This is a real risk.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.529
In any case it would, in a way, be a victory
for Russia.

00:11:45.529 --> 00:11:48.430
A less clear victory, but ultimately a victory.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.660
They would have annexed much of Ukraine and,
in the end, the international community would

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.450
not have done much beyond the initial flurry
of action to prevent it.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:00.510
("Beijing is watching closely, to see the
price Russia pays, or the reward it receives,

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:01.510
for its aggression.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:04.459
What's happening in Europe today may happen
in Asia tomorrow."

00:12:04.459 --> 00:12:06.880
Jens Stoltenberg, NATO Secretary General)

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:10.970
And, take note, because if the arms supply
to Ukraine is not increased this scenario

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:11.970
is quite likely...

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.000
And perhaps the best way out for Russia and
perhaps also for Vladimir Putin himself.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:20.260
That is why some allies, such as Germany or
France, two countries that are not particularly

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.300
comfortable with the war – I’ll leave
it to you to guess the reasons – have been

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:30.510
convinced of another alternative, the third
possibility to put an end to the fighting.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:33.900
(3.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.570
THINKING 2024)

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:41.019
In 2024 there are elections in Russia...

00:12:41.019 --> 00:12:45.190
And that is why Putin and his entourage could
be the most interested in reaching a solution

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.250
to the conflict before that date.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:52.519
Lest a military and economic setback, therefore,
call into question his continuity in the top

00:12:52.519 --> 00:12:53.639
job in the Kremlin.

00:12:53.639 --> 00:12:55.850
That is, if the war is not over...

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.350
Many Russian circles could push to get a failed
president out of the way in order to place

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.089
a new leader at the helm...

00:13:02.089 --> 00:13:05.579
Taking advantage of what would technically
be the end of the Russian president's term.

00:13:05.579 --> 00:13:09.589
Well, to avoid such a scenario, Putin might
be willing to negotiate and make concessions.

00:13:09.589 --> 00:13:14.140
That at least is what both French President,
Emmanuel Macron, and German Chancellor, Olaf

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.760
Scholz, seem to think.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:19.310
But for all this to be possible, Ukraine must
be in a position to harm Russia...

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.990
This requires the rapid delivery of many more
weapons.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.079
Leopards, tanks?

00:13:23.079 --> 00:13:25.220
Well, that's the way it's going.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:29.010
("What we need now is for Ukraine to launch
a military offensive that pushes back the

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:33.001
Russian front to open the way for a return
to negotiations" Emmanuel Macron, President

00:13:33.001 --> 00:13:34.001
of France)

00:13:34.001 --> 00:13:38.610
And it might not even be necessary to wait
until 2024.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:45.220
A Ukrainian offensive in the southeast capable
of reaching the Sea of Azov, recapturing the

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.740
entire Zaporizhia area and putting Crimea
within artillery range, could be enough to

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:51.180
force a negotiation.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.089
This is what we could call the Big Bang action.

00:13:54.089 --> 00:13:58.170
Now, if a negotiated exit is reached...

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.430
Can we really trust Russia to keep its side
of the bargain?

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.339
Well, the truth is that history tells us that
we can’t.

00:14:03.339 --> 00:14:05.160
Ukraine, in fact, is a good example.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:10.050
Don't forget that Russia itself guaranteed,
in the Budapest Memorandum, the security and

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:14.570
complete sovereignty of Ukraine – including
Crimea – in exchange for Ukraine's surrender

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:15.820
of its nuclear weapons.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:20.139
Because, remember that upon the dissolution
of the Soviet Union, Ukraine became the third

00:14:20.139 --> 00:14:24.459
most heavily nuclear-armed country in the
world.

00:14:24.459 --> 00:14:29.770
Therefore, in exchange for these possible
negotiations, Western countries would give

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:34.230
Ukraine much more tangible security: enough
military equipment to discourage any further

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:38.270
Russian aggression in the future: we are talking
about modern armored vehicles, missiles, an

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.850
air force, and whatever else is necessary.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.420
An agreement with NATO could even be considered.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:47.360
And since we would be talking about an agreed
exit, the country could try to get back on

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.529
track.

00:14:50.529 --> 00:14:54.820
In this way, Ukraine could be shielded and
have a future in exchange for certain concessions

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:58.990
in an agreement that, although bad, would
be much more acceptable than the previous

00:14:58.990 --> 00:14:59.990
scenario.

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:02.851
This seems to be, at least, the perception
of the Paris-Berlin tandem, which, according

00:15:02.851 --> 00:15:06.089
to what they say today, London does not see
as a bad thing either.

00:15:06.089 --> 00:15:10.820
What’s more, Ukraine would not run the risk
of what could happen in 2025 if there were

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:12.149
a change in the White House.

00:15:12.149 --> 00:15:16.790
And, take note, because as of today this may
be by far the most likely end to the war.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.009
Of course, there is still another possible
path.

00:15:19.009 --> 00:15:24.160
One with many supporters in Ukraine, Poland,
the Baltic States and, also, the United States

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.160
of America.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:26.160
What am I talking about?

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:27.160
Well...

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.490
We're going to take a look right now.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.959
(4.

00:15:31.959 --> 00:15:35.460
VICTORY AT ANY PRICE)

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:41.100
2023 started with very good news for Ukraine:
We are talking about the commitment to deliver

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:45.560
dozens and dozens, hundreds of armored vehicles
among other equipment...

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.279
Including modern tanks.

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:53.430
We're talking, Bradleys, Strykers, Marders,
AMX-10; Challenger II, Leopards, Patriot Batteries,

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.139
etcetera, etcetera, etcetera.

00:15:55.139 --> 00:16:00.009
If these deliveries are sustained and increased
over time, the course of the war could change

00:16:00.009 --> 00:16:01.009
completely.

00:16:01.009 --> 00:16:04.460
Especially if more HIMARS, more tanks and
long-range missiles are delivered.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.819
Let alone if they were provided with more
and better aircraft and drones.

00:16:07.819 --> 00:16:13.009
And let's see, initially the delivery of weapons
had been very restrained in order, for example,

00:16:13.009 --> 00:16:17.700
not to have to accept a defeat against Russia
if Ukraine finally did not withstand the challenge.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.940
And, what can I say, it makes perfect sense,
otherwise NATO would have been badly damaged

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.899
and the leadership of the United States would
have been called into question.

00:16:24.899 --> 00:16:28.570
Of course, the implications for the rest of
the world would have been enormous.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:32.710
Now, however, things are completely different.

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:39.779
You see, according to many reports, the Russian
army may be exhausted and under-equipped.

00:16:39.779 --> 00:16:43.720
Which would explain why they are having such
a hard time pulling off any offensive.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:47.800
It is true that Russia has sent many new men
thanks to conscription, but it is also true

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:51.440
that the combat strength of these units does
not seem particularly high.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.970
That is why a succession of strong counterattacks
by the Ukrainian army could blow up the Russian

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:56.970
defense lines.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.790
In other words, there may be a chance to go
all out, defeat Russia and force its army

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:04.839
to retreat and even leave Ukraine, perhaps
with the sole exception of Crimea.

00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:09.120
In so doing, the damage to the Putin regime
would be potentially irreparable.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:12.190
And the question is, but what would it take
to achieve that?

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:15.230
Much more extensive and more determined military
support.

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:19.250
Of course, on the one hand, this possibility
would put the nuclear risk back on the table,

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.079
but we already told you about that in a past
video here on VisualPolitik.

00:17:22.079 --> 00:17:24.990
We told you why Moscow was unlikely to resort
to that possibility.

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.970
Basically because it would gain nothing.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.130
But naturally the risk is still there.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:32.230
Particularly because this scenario would put
the Russian leader in check.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:36.410
Obviously losing a war against a much smaller
country with far fewer resources is not a

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:41.650
good thing, even more so when military modernization
and making Russia a strong and great country

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:45.780
again was the Putin regime's No. 1 priority
for more than two decades.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:50.120
What’s more, if history tells us anything,
it is that it is very difficult for a regime

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.170
to survive when it loses a war.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.500
And do you know what?

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.909
Despite all the casualties and all the pain
suffered.

00:17:59.909 --> 00:18:03.260
This is the option with the most supporters
right now in Ukraine.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:08.580
(Every Ukrainian has lost someone in the past
year.

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:15.669
A father, a son, a brother, a mother, a daughter,
a sister.

00:18:15.669 --> 00:18:17.450
A loved one.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.990
A close friend, colleague, neighbor, acquaintance.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:25.919
So there you have it VisualPolitik viewers,
these are the four possible scenarios for

00:18:25.919 --> 00:18:27.780
us to see the Ukrainian war end.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:32.610
You can see that in any case the "best" ways
out seem to call for a lot more weapons being

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.340
delivered to the Ukrainian government.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:37.030
This is something that almost everyone seems
to have understood.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:38.700
Even Olaf Scholz himself.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.430
So now it's your turn:

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.740
Which strategy do you think is the most important
to follow?

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.640
What would you do if you were calling the
shots?

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.059
Leave us your answer in the comments and let's
open a debate.

00:18:48.059 --> 00:18:51.059
And now, if you found this video interesting,
don't forget to like and subscribe to VisualPolitik.

00:18:51.059 --> 00:18:52.540
All the best and see you next time.

